import Mathlib

namespace Erdos219

/-
# Problem Description

Erdős Problem 219. Are there arbitrarily long arithmetic progressions of primes?
`erdos_219` proves that there are.

The affirmative answer is the Green--Tao theorem [GrTa08]. Below,
`primeArithmeticProgressions` is the set of nonempty arithmetic progressions all of whose
members are prime, and the statement says that for every `N` some such progression has at
least `N` terms.

The proof formalised here is a full development of the Green--Tao theorem, and is the largest
dependency closure in this repository.

The formalisation is by plby (github.com/plby/lean-proofs),
`src/latest/ErdosProblems/Erdos219.lean` together with the modules of its import closure.
Those files are concatenated here in dependency order, with their project-internal imports
removed so that `Mathlib` is the only import, each module's contents kept in a `section`
carrying its own `open` lines, and the whole wrapped once in `namespace Erdos219` with the
upstream trust-base print line removed. No mathematical content is changed.
-/

